Test the identities with \(\alpha = 30^{\circ}\), where you know \(2\alpha = 60^{\circ}\):
\(2\sin 30^{\circ}\cos 30^{\circ} = 2\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} = \sin 60^{\circ}\);
\(1 - 2\sin^{2}30^{\circ} = 1 - \frac{1}{2} = \frac{1}{2} = \cos 60^{\circ}\);
\(\frac{2\tan 30^{\circ}}{1 - \tan^{2}30^{\circ}} = \frac{2/\sqrt{3}}{2/3} = \sqrt{3} = \tan 60^{\circ}\).
Such a quick test helps you recall a formula correctly in the exam.
